;;; Next Prime
;;;
;;; Original program from the HP 32s manual, adapted to HP 42s.
;;;
;;; Take any positive integer greater than 3. If the number is prime, return the input value.
;;; If the input is not prime, return the first prime larger than the input.
;;;
;;; The program identifies non-prime numbers by exhaustively trying all possible factors.
;;; If the number is not prime, the program adds 2 (assuring that the value is still odd) and tests
;;; to see if it has found a prime. The process continues until a prime is found.
;;;
;;; Registers:
;;; R00 = P
;;; R01 = D

LBL "NEXTP"
GTO 00          ; P

LBL 01          ; LBL Y
CLST
RCL 00          ; VIEW P
STOP

LBL 02          ; LBL Z
2
RCL+ 00         ; RCL+ P

LBL 00          ; LBL P
STO 00          ; STO P
2
/
FP
0
X=Y?
1
STO+ 00         ; STO+ P
3
STO 01          ; STO D

LBL 03          ; LBL X
RCL 00          ; RCL P
RCL / 01        ; RCL/ D
FP
X=0?
GTO 02          ; GTO Z
RCL 00          ; RCL P
SQRT
RCL 01          ; RCL D
X>Y?
GTO 01          ; GTO Y
2
STO+ 01         ; STO+ D
GTO 03          ; GTO X
